1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,946
Play two notes that are
almost the same, both at once.

2
00:00:03,946 --> 00:00:06,801
The sound swells and
fades, again and again.

3
00:00:07,201 --> 00:00:11,395
Diya heard this tonight, when two
phones rang with almost the same tone.

4
00:00:11,795 --> 00:00:14,143
Each tone alone is a steady wave.

5
00:00:14,143 --> 00:00:16,956
Add the two, and a slow wobble appears.

6
00:00:16,956 --> 00:00:18,919
Loud, soft, loud, soft.

7
00:00:19,319 --> 00:00:21,383
Where does that wobble come from?

8
00:00:21,383 --> 00:00:24,149
Diya's guess: inside
the sum hides a product.

9
00:00:24,649 --> 00:00:25,682
She is right.

10
00:00:25,682 --> 00:00:28,876
Today we turn sums into
products, and back again.

11
00:00:29,526 --> 00:00:31,640
Here is the idea in one picture.

12
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:37,031
On the unit circle, mark point P
at angle x, and point Q at angle y.

13
00:00:37,431 --> 00:00:39,367
P is at cos x, sine x.

14
00:00:39,367 --> 00:00:41,303
Q is at cos y, sine y.

15
00:00:41,303 --> 00:00:44,999
Add them like two moves
on a map, and you reach R.

16
00:00:45,399 --> 00:00:49,774
R points in the middle direction,
the half sum, x plus y over two.

17
00:00:50,174 --> 00:00:54,521
Its distance from the centre is two
cos of the half difference, x minus

18
00:00:54,521 --> 00:00:55,459
y over two.

19
00:00:55,859 --> 00:01:01,156
So how far R is across, cos x plus
cos y, equals two cos of the half sum,

20
00:01:01,156 --> 00:01:03,513
times cos of the half difference.

21
00:01:03,513 --> 00:01:05,286
A sum became a product.

22
00:01:05,936 --> 00:01:07,386
Watch it stay true.

23
00:01:07,386 --> 00:01:10,497
Keep x at seventy
degrees, and slide y down.

24
00:01:10,897 --> 00:01:14,166
Left side and right side
are worked out separately.

25
00:01:14,166 --> 00:01:15,566
They never disagree.

26
00:01:15,966 --> 00:01:20,416
When y comes back up to x, the half
difference is zero, and the answer

27
00:01:20,416 --> 00:01:21,507
is two cos x.

28
00:01:22,157 --> 00:01:25,123
Now let us prove it with
algebra, in small steps.

29
00:01:25,473 --> 00:01:30,475
From episode thirty three: cos of A
plus B is cos A cos B, minus sine A

30
00:01:30,475 --> 00:01:31,375
sine B.

31
00:01:31,972 --> 00:01:36,356
And cos of A minus B is cos
A cos B, plus sine A sine B.

32
00:01:37,106 --> 00:01:38,582
Add the two lines.

33
00:01:38,582 --> 00:01:40,270
The sine parts cancel.

34
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:42,256
Two cos A cos B is left.

35
00:01:43,006 --> 00:01:44,006
Now rename.

36
00:01:44,006 --> 00:01:46,834
Call A plus B x, and A minus B y.

37
00:01:46,834 --> 00:01:49,760
Adding them, A is x plus y over two.

38
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:53,012
Subtracting them, B is x minus y over two.

39
00:01:53,762 --> 00:01:55,138
Put these back in.

40
00:01:55,138 --> 00:01:59,763
cos x plus cos y equals two cos of
the half sum, times cos of the half

41
00:01:59,763 --> 00:02:00,663
difference.

42
00:02:01,365 --> 00:02:04,733
The same trick on the sine
formulas gives three more.

43
00:02:05,133 --> 00:02:09,865
sine x plus sine y: two sine of the
half sum, cos of the half difference.

44
00:02:10,265 --> 00:02:15,340
sine x minus sine y: two cos of the
half sum, sine of the half difference.

45
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:20,639
And cos x minus cos y: minus two sine
of the half sum, sine of the half

46
00:02:20,639 --> 00:02:21,539
difference.

47
00:02:21,513 --> 00:02:22,813
Watch that minus.

48
00:02:23,463 --> 00:02:25,433
Now back to Diya's two tones.

49
00:02:25,783 --> 00:02:28,837
Tone one is cos twelve t, where t is time.

50
00:02:28,837 --> 00:02:31,832
Tone two is cos eleven t, a little slower.

51
00:02:32,232 --> 00:02:37,053
By our formula, their sum is two cos
of eleven point five t, times cos

52
00:02:37,053 --> 00:02:38,018
of half t.

53
00:02:38,418 --> 00:02:40,643
The fast part is the note you hear.

54
00:02:40,643 --> 00:02:43,559
The slow part, cos of
half t, is the wobble.

55
00:02:43,959 --> 00:02:46,306
Now pull the second tone further away.

56
00:02:46,706 --> 00:02:49,306
The bigger the gap, the faster the wobble.

57
00:02:49,306 --> 00:02:51,321
With no gap, no wobble at all.

58
00:02:51,321 --> 00:02:54,072
That is a beat: a sum
written as a product.

59
00:02:54,722 --> 00:02:55,861
Side by side.

60
00:02:55,861 --> 00:02:58,519
Sum to product turns plus into times.

61
00:02:58,519 --> 00:03:01,937
Use it to factorise, or
to simplify a fraction.

62
00:03:02,337 --> 00:03:04,924
Product to sum turns times into plus.

63
00:03:04,924 --> 00:03:08,045
Use it to break a product
into simple pieces.

64
00:03:08,645 --> 00:03:09,749
Now you try.

65
00:03:09,749 --> 00:03:12,524
Two sine three x cos x is a product.

66
00:03:12,524 --> 00:03:14,131
Which way do we go?

67
00:03:14,131 --> 00:03:15,502
Pause and decide.

68
00:03:18,702 --> 00:03:19,957
Product to sum!

69
00:03:19,957 --> 00:03:24,656
Two sine A cos B is sine of A
plus B, plus sine of A minus B.

70
00:03:24,656 --> 00:03:27,240
So, sine four x plus sine two x.

71
00:03:27,890 --> 00:03:28,846
Remember this.

72
00:03:28,846 --> 00:03:30,534
Half sum, half difference.

73
00:03:30,534 --> 00:03:32,143
That is the whole secret.

74
00:03:32,843 --> 00:03:34,578
Now, one worked example.

75
00:03:34,928 --> 00:03:40,137
Find the exact value of sine seventy
five degrees plus sine fifteen degrees.

76
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:41,537
Step one.

77
00:03:41,423 --> 00:03:46,672
sine x plus sine y is two sine of the half
sum, times cos of the half difference.

78
00:03:47,422 --> 00:03:48,322
Step two.

79
00:03:48,215 --> 00:03:51,752
The half sum of seventy five
and fifteen is forty five.

80
00:03:51,752 --> 00:03:53,733
The half difference is thirty.

81
00:03:54,483 --> 00:03:55,389
Step three.

82
00:03:55,389 --> 00:03:58,946
So the sum is two sine forty
five, times cos thirty.

83
00:03:59,696 --> 00:04:00,596
Step four.

84
00:04:00,554 --> 00:04:05,389
Two, times root two over two, times
root three over two, is root six over

85
00:04:05,389 --> 00:04:06,289
two.

86
00:04:06,643 --> 00:04:11,044
On the circle, R points at forty
five degrees, and its height is about

87
00:04:11,044 --> 00:04:12,377
one point two two.

88
00:04:13,027 --> 00:04:14,492
Now, the exam trap.

89
00:04:14,842 --> 00:04:17,838
cos eighty degrees minus
cos twenty degrees.

90
00:04:17,838 --> 00:04:21,585
Many students write two sine
fifty, times sine thirty.

91
00:04:21,985 --> 00:04:26,817
But cos eighty is smaller than cos
twenty, so the answer must be negative.

92
00:04:26,817 --> 00:04:31,343
The right answer starts with a minus:
minus two sine fifty sine thirty,

93
00:04:31,343 --> 00:04:32,816
or minus sine fifty.

94
00:04:33,466 --> 00:04:35,020
Where is this asked?

95
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:39,745
In JEE Main, as short questions that
simplify sums and products of sines

96
00:04:39,745 --> 00:04:40,756
and cosines.

97
00:04:41,356 --> 00:04:42,669
Exam level now.

98
00:04:42,669 --> 00:04:44,905
Find cos of alpha plus beta.

99
00:04:44,905 --> 00:04:46,274
Pause and solve.

100
00:04:51,674 --> 00:04:53,130
The answer is B.

101
00:04:53,130 --> 00:04:54,689
Five over thirteen.

102
00:04:55,189 --> 00:04:57,073
Turn both sums into products.

103
00:04:57,073 --> 00:04:59,495
Both share cos of the half difference.

104
00:04:59,995 --> 00:05:00,966
Divide them.

105
00:05:00,966 --> 00:05:05,788
The cos and the twos cancel, so tan
of the half sum is one third over one

106
00:05:05,788 --> 00:05:07,739
half, which is two thirds.

107
00:05:08,239 --> 00:05:12,072
Then cos of alpha plus beta
is cos of twice the half sum.

108
00:05:12,072 --> 00:05:16,844
One minus four ninths, over one plus
four ninths, is five over thirteen.

109
00:05:17,444 --> 00:05:18,903
Here is your recap.

110
00:05:18,903 --> 00:05:20,402
Screenshot this card.

111
00:05:23,602 --> 00:05:26,439
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

112
00:05:26,839 --> 00:05:27,739
One.

113
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:30,947
Write cos four x plus
cos two x as a product.

114
00:05:31,847 --> 00:05:32,747
Two.

115
00:05:32,416 --> 00:05:37,864
Find the exact value of sine seventy
five degrees minus sine fifteen degrees.

116
00:05:38,764 --> 00:05:39,664
Three.

117
00:05:39,462 --> 00:05:42,549
Turn two cos five x cos x into a sum.

118
00:05:43,649 --> 00:05:47,377
Next time: when is the tyre
valve exactly at half height?

119
00:05:47,377 --> 00:05:50,101
Not once, but again and again, forever.

120
00:05:50,101 --> 00:05:51,618
Trigonometric equations.
